From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 22:58:06 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 14/19] fix(gastown): fail closed on an unreadable session
 roster and stage the reaper rollout (gcp-z2z)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Mayor review of PR #5 @ 54a8b7b: CHANGES_REQUESTED on two defects. The design
and gates 1-3 stand; these are the two fixes, nothing wider.

1. session_is_live failed OPEN. A `gc session list` that errored fell back to
   {"sessions":[]}, and malformed JSON drove jq -e non-zero — both resolved to
   NOT LIVE, so gate 4 silently vanished on exactly the reads that failed and
   the reap proceeded against a live polecat. That is the inverted form of the
   rule gcp-g98 just landed in the witness one step away in the same formula:
   a confirmation read that fails is not proof of absence.

   Replaced with a tri-state `session_state` printing live | absent |
   unconfirmed. The roster is seeded `unconfirmed` and promoted only by a read
   that exited 0, wrote a non-empty file, and parsed with `.sessions` an array;
   a per-session jq failure or an unrecognized verdict degrades the same way.
   `unconfirmed` skips the worktree and logs worktree_owner_unconfirmed, so no
   failed read has a route to a removal. The empty-owner path is unchanged
   (`absent`) — the review recorded that as a known limit, not a fix.

2. No staged rollout. pre_start passed no --dry-run, so real removal began the
   moment the city moved off its pin, while city.toml deliberately holds the
   native gascity reaper in dry-run until gc-zxxy is answered. Real removal is
   now opt-in behind --no-dry-run, DRY_RUN defaults to 1, and the witness
   pre_start does not pass it — so the reaper reports its would-reap set and
   removes nothing until an operator flips it. --dry-run still works.

Docs follow the behavior: agent.toml, the witness prompt, and the patrol step
all state that the reaper is in dry-run and how the flip is made, and the event
table gains worktree_reap_pending and worktree_owner_unconfirmed rows.

Tests: real removal is opt-in (bare invocation removes nothing, pre_start
carries no opt-in), and an unreadable roster — command failure AND unparseable
output — skips a worktree whose owner is live, with a third case proving a
clean roster still reaps so the guard is not just inertness. Verified red
against 54a8b7b: the pre-fix script reaps a live-owned worktree when the roster
read fails.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
